  +| review 2026-11-09 (PR #467) | medium | `harnessNote` (`cli/src/agent.ts`) recognises Nexus's own user-role notes by their `[Nexus:` / `[Nexus ` text prefix, so an operator message beginning with that text is treated as a harness note (left out of earlier task requests in compaction and of the findings request). Switching to provenance (the message-level marker the skill note gets for item 11) needs a migration for the prefix-only notes in sessions saved by v1.1.3 | FIXED (WP-1308). Every user-role note Nexus writes (continuation, recovery, parser notices, cut-off reply, empty reply, subagent recovery) is created through `harnessNoteMessage` with the message-level marker `harness: "note"` (the skill note keeps `"skill-note"`); `isHarnessNote` (`cli/src/harness_notes.ts`) is the only recogniser, and compaction (earlier task requests and the current request), the findings request, the TUI objective and the sidecar history all use it, so an operator message beginning `[Nexus:` stays a request. Saved sessions are migrated on load by `withHarnessProvenance` (the three restore paths in `agent.ts` and the sidecar history; no schema bump, as for the skill note, because the marker is an optional field older readers ignore). **Legacy rule, chosen conservatively:** an unmarked user message is migrated only when it matches the exact wording of each kind of note a v1.1.3 Nexus pushed (`[Nexus recovery N/M] You have `, `[Nexus continuation N/M] The operator's acceptance requirements are still open: `, `[Nexus: your reply was empty: no text and no tool call.`, `[Nexus: your previous reply was cut off at `, the parser notices `[Nexus: Malformed native tool call dropped`, `[Nexus: Tool "x" is not offered on this request`, `[Nexus: Tool call "x" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair`, and the two `[Nexus] ` recovery notes for compaction re-reads and repeated polls) and it follows an assistant message, a tool result or another note (never the first message; after an unmarked user message only the cut-off note qualifies, because a cut-off reply is discarded before any assistant message is written). The migration is idempotent (marked messages are untouched). Accepted ambiguity: a v1.1.3 operator message that copies one of those notes verbatim after a model reply is indistinguishable from the note and is migrated; any other text with the prefix, or containing a note, is not. A bare `[Nexus:` prefix is not enough, so the false-positive window is limited to pasted verbatim notes in already-saved sessions, and new messages are never affected. Tests: `cli/test/harness_provenance.test.ts` (operator prefix kept in compaction and findings request; v1.1.3 session migrated and loading twice identical; new notes marked and surviving save/load; resembling operator text not migrated), with `cli/test/context_convergence.test.ts` (CTX-06, updated: notes carry the marker, prefixed operator text is a request), `cli/test/skill_injection.test.ts`, `cli/test/skill_ranking.test.ts` |
